<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=oil-lamp">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Energy and power</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oil lamp</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 10,300–8000 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An oil lamp is a lamp that burns an oil-based fuel, drawn up a textile wick from a container, in the same way as a candle burns solid fuel. Curved stone lamps have been found at sites dated to the 10th millennium BCE, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesolithic">Mesolithic</a>, and the first manufactured red pottery lamps appeared in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcolithic">Chalcolithic</a>. Fuels included olive, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sesame">sesame</a> and nut oils and animal fats. The Argand lamp of 1780 quickly replaced the old basic form, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerosene">kerosene</a> lamp replaced that from about 1850.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oil-lamp.jpg" alt="Oil lamp" width="330" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Combirom2 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Group_of_ancient_hellenistic_an_roan_oil_lamps.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>10th millennium BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Mesolithic sites (stone lamps; no single place named)</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Some archaeologists claim shell lamps existed more than 6,000 years ago, and the oldest stone oil lamp is said to come from Lascaux, in a cave inhabited 10,000 to 15,000 years ago.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/control-of-fire">Control of fire<span>c. 1 million years ago</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/candle">Candle<span>7th century BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=oil-lamp">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
